{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1097479-lore-of-the-flesh-demon-the-fallen","id":1097479,"title":"Lore of the Flesh (Demon The Fallen)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-27T03:50:52-07:00","id":1097479,"title":"Lore of the Flesh (Demon The Fallen)","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>** Manipulate Nerves</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Like Body Control, this evocation allows the demon to manipulate a subject\u2019s nervous system. Strength and reflexes can be enhanced, senses can be dulled or sharpened, or the person can </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">be </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">subjected to waves of intense pleasure or pain. </span><br /> <b>System:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Roll Intelligence </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">+ </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Medicine. The difficulty is determined </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">by </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">the complexity of the intended effect. Reducing the effects of pain is difficulty 6, while increasing the speed of a person\u2019s reflexes (increasing his Dexterity) is </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">7 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">or </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">8. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Sharpening a person\u2019s senses (or dulling them) might require a difficulty of 9 or more. Each success increases or decreases a relevant physical trait or wound penalty </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">by </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">one, as appropriate for the effort. The effects of this evocation last for the duration of the scene. To perform this evocation on another individual, the demon must be able to make physical contact, and a resisted Willpower (difficulty 8) can be made to counteract your character\u2019s effort. </span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#686868\">So basically, with this you could reduce wound penalties(1 per success) or increase and decrease Dexterity. or sharpen and dull senses, what about Strength ? it mentions Strength in the description but not in the system, does this power cover strength aswell ? if that's the case, that kinda trumps the physical edge of the rank 3 power(leaving aside the mental attributes that can be risen). so can it or not ?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#686868\">and how exactly would the effects be if i decide to dull someone's senses ? does it basically reduce perception trait by 1 per success ? or ?</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#686868\">next, if i decide to pump a friend's attributes, and he's not willing to resist. does that negate the need for that resistance willpower roll ?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#686868\">Are the powers of this lore considered reflexive to activate ? for example, could i use lore of the flesh rank 2 above + make a dodge/parry/block/attack attempt ? </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *** Manipulate Flesh </div> </div> </div></b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\">This evocation allows the demon to manipulate a subject\u2019s physical form (be it her own or another\u2019s), adding muscle mass, increasing bone density or expanding mental faculties. </span><br /> <b>System:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Roll Intelligence </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">+ </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Medicine. Each success is a point that can be added to any of the subject\u2019s Physical or Mental Attributes. There is a risk, however. Compare the total number of successes to the subject\u2019s Stamina. Any excess successes are suffered as bashing damage due to system shock. This damage cannot be soaked. To perform this evocation on another individual, the demonmust be able to make physical contact, and the individual can attempt to counteract its effects -the Storyteller makes a Willpower roll (difficulty 8). </span> </div> </div> </div>This power does not state any difficulty, do i go with 6 ?<br /> <br /> And can i also use this to /reduce/ someone's muscle mass, bone density or mental faculties ? <br /> <br /> <u><b>Also for both powers, what is the limit per trait i can raise ? can i raise them up to 10 maximum or ?</b></u>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12206,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","user":"onedayumay","date":". 05-27-2017, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T08:29:36-07:00","id":1097531,"title":"","content":"For the first question; the rules mention a physical trait. This covers strength. And the resisted roll <i>can</i> be made, which is not a <i>requirement</i>. Dulling would be a reduction of traits instead of increasing them. The use of this Lore is not considered to be a reflexive action, just like with any other power that's not explicitly stated to be a reflexive action.<br /> <br /> Manipulate Flesh cannot be used to <i>reduce</i> Attributes, since it only states that you can add the successes. I'd go with the usual difficulty 6, since it's a more potent power than the two-dot version.<br /> <br /> As for the trait limit, no limit is given. No statted Demon has attributes above 5 (even the Earthbound), but I'd allow temporary increases above the normal maximum of 5 for the duration of the scene (that's the duration as per the FAQ in the Player's Guide), with a few caveats:<br /> <br /> - 10 is the maximum.<br /> - Successes by multiple uses are not cumulative.<br /> - If you roll more successes than on a similar roll you can replace your old boost by the new one.<br /> - Buffing Stamina does not increase the number at which you suffer system shock.<br /> - You don't suffer damage by going above your Stamina that you already have. Example: you have Stamina 3. First you roll 4 successes, making you suffer 1 damage, then on a second roll you roll 5 successes, which has you suffer only 1 damage since you already suffered 1 damage by rolling 1 success above your Stamina.<br /> - Increasing Intelligence allows you to roll more dice for the power, with the risk of rolling way over your Stamina on subsequent rolls.<br /> - The damage suffered by this power cannot be healed as it remains in effect. After that it can be healed as normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T09:16:52-07:00","id":1097549,"title":"","content":"Alright understood, i play in a community where we have a house rule that denies multiple applications of this lore, aka you can't stack successes. <br /> But that does not mean that i cant raise each attribute seperately correct ? example: i use Manipulate Nerves (rank 2) to raise my reflexes(Dexterity) and score 5 successes. once im done i'll use use the same power to increase my Strength with a different roll, but once only. that should be fine right ? thanks for the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T09:43:11-07:00","id":1097561,"title":"","content":"Sure, you can raise all six of them individually. You just have to be careful about it because this will hurt you down the line. The successes between the various Attributes won't add up (so if you increase your Strengh by 2 and your Dexterity by 3 you won't get into trouble if you have Stamina 3), so feel free to cast in advance if your Stamina is high enough.<br /> <br /> Also, the houserule for &quot;you have only one shot at it&quot; is a smart one, since otherwise people would just keep rolling until they're demonic demigods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}